{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/examples/ingress.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:37:52.945472Z","id":"af3548cce9032bcdec101ff548e42f017999f7a73178eb133f2cd3365673d287","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs:44 sets MAX_WAIT_SECS to 3600, and the fleet's own proxy gives up only after MAX_WAIT_SECS + 60 (crates/clax-fleet/src/proxy.rs:64-67) for exactly this reason. ingress-nginx's proxy-read-timeout is the time between two reads from the upstream; a long poll that sends nothing until it answers at 3600 s can be cut by nginx with a 504 at the same moment, so the client sees a gateway error instead of the server's 'still waiting' answer.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"0baf8f8e4379c76cce7751baa01b0d5a7931bd03357de325dfb6213153310c98"},"suggested_fix":"Set proxy-read-timeout and proxy-send-timeout to 3700 (above MAX_WAIT_SECS + 60), with a comment naming the constant they must exceed, and say so in docs/kubernetes.md, Ingress, DNS and TLS.","summary":"The example's 3600 s proxy read timeout equals the longest long poll, so a question wait that runs its full hour races the controller's timeout","tags":["review","review:k8s-ergonomics-2026-11-02","session:claude-code:cee68005-68c6-43ca-8000-8b393af6e6ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/examples/ingress.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:42:09.707635Z","id":"3ef8ad2cec175367f907f3613e882c94afba90a604318211af2ad6ea5f083494","body":{"detail":"deploy/k8s/examples/ingress.yaml:12-13 set proxy-read-timeout and proxy-send-timeout to \"3600\"; crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs:44 `pub const MAX_WAIT_SECS: u64 = 3600`, and the poll handler (questions.rs:476-485) returns one JSON body after up to that wait; crates/clax-fleet/src/proxy.rs:64-67 gives up only after MAX_WAIT_SECS + 60. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"af3548cce9032bcdec101ff548e42f017999f7a73178eb133f2cd3365673d287","summary":"confirmed: the example's 3600 s read timeout equals MAX_WAIT_SECS, whereas the fleet's own proxy waits MAX_WAIT_SECS + 60","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:cee68005-68c6-43ca-8000-8b393af6e6ea"]}}
